specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md-544-In multi-tool scenarios, multiple ToolEntry objects may appear between the ThinkingEntry and AssistantEntry. The tool execution loop (Section 9) may produce additional entries.
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md-545-
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:546:- A reply with no tool calls and no thinking produces, in order, the user entry, the assistant entry opened empty, one `entry_delta` per text chunk, its `entry_commit`, and `stream_end` ([validated by: sends the user entry, then the assistant entry, its delta, its commit and stream_end](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L196)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:547:- A thinking block is committed before the assistant entry that follows it is opened, so the two never interleave ([validated by: commits the thinking entry before the assistant entry opens](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L222)).
